    <DataNode elementId="CPD-8922" textLabel="(+)-sesamin" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="PEYUIKBAABKQKQ-AFHBHXEDSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="205.83229064941406" centerY="1052.6748046875" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, nilo-poyanco">Sesamin is a lignan characterized from sesame oil. It has been reported to inhibit |FRAME: MONOMER-12526| activity and hence the conversion of |FRAME: CPD-8120| to |FRAME: ARACHIDONIC_ACID|. Sesamin can also inhibit |FRAME: MONOMER-16595 &quot;Acyl-CoA:lysophosphatidylcholine acyltransferase&quot;| (LPCAT) activity in the filamentous fungus |FRAME: TAX-64518| |CITS: [11171183]|. LPCAT is responsible for the acylation of sn-1-acyl-lysophosphatidylcholine to yield phosphatidylcholine.</Comment>
